wamr provides CMake target iwasm::vmlib:

    find_package(iwasm CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE iwasm::vmlib)

Headers:

    #include "wasm_export.h"
    #include "wasm_c_api.h"
    #include "lib_export.h"

Default (no features) is fast interpreter only:

    vcpkg install wamr

Features:

    classic-interp - classic interpreter instead of fast (saves ~2x memory, ~0.5x speed)
        vcpkg install wamr[classic-interp]
        # cmake: -DWAMR_BUILD_FAST_INTERP=0 (INVERTED)

    aot - enable AOT runtime (requires wamrc to compile .wasm -> .aot)
        vcpkg install wamr[aot]
        wamrc -o app.aot app.wasm
        iwasm app.aot   # via libiwasm: wasm_runtime_load() handles both .wasm and .aot

    fast-jit - enable Fast JIT (asmjit/zydis, ~50% of AOT speed, not on Windows)
        vcpkg install wamr[fast-jit]
        # Linux/macOS only; on Windows upstream forces FAST_JIT=0

Combine:

    vcpkg install wamr[aot,fast-jit]          # AOT + Fast JIT
    vcpkg install wamr[aot,classic-interp]    # AOT + classic interpreter
